    decisions: ["Use a single student information system as the system of record. Other modules hold only references and cached views, so there is exactly one place to correct a name, section or guardian.","Combine RBAC for coarse roles with relationship-based checks such as guardian-of and teaches-section. Roles alone cannot express 'a parent sees only their own child'.","Use a shared-schema multi-tenant design with tenant_id and row-level security for small schools, and allow dedicated databases for large universities with data-residency or contract needs.","Model results as immutable, versioned, approval-gated records rather than editable rows, which keeps every grade change auditable.","Treat payment state as driven by gateway webhooks and daily reconciliation, never by the client redirect, and keep money in a double-entry ledger."],
    pitfalls: ["Marking a fee as paid on the browser redirect, which leads to false receipts when the payment later fails, or to double charges when users retry.","Letting teachers edit published marks directly, which destroys the audit trail and invites disputes and tampering.","Sending a child's attendance or results to a phone number that has not been verified as the guardian's, or ignoring verifiable parental consent required under India's DPDP Act for users under 18.","Re-running the full timetable solver mid-term for one teacher's leave, which reshuffles every class; handle it with substitutions instead.","Giving administrators raw database access for reports instead of masked, role-scoped datasets."],
